; draw_control_chars, the one variable no other LineEdit fixture sets. No font can shape the
; mid-string U+0001. With the flag on it draws as a hex-code box that takes width, pushing "after"
; right. Treating it as ordinary text (an average-glyph-width advance instead of dropping or
; boxing it) is invisible to a diff that checks only the surrounding glyphs' ink.

